  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BUILDING A COLLABORATIVE FOUNDATION FOR EVIDENCE-BASED SAIGA ANTELOPE CONSERVATION</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE USFWS SPECIES CONSERVATION CATALYST FUND IS A UNIQUE OPPORTUNITY TO BUILD BOTH A SYSTEMIC UNDERSTANDING OF THE DRIVERS AND LEVERAGE POINTS FOR SAIGA USE AND TRADE, AND TO BUILD A FOUNDATION FOR LONG-TERM COLLABORATIVE NETWORKS TO IMPLEMENT, AND ADAPTIVELY MANAGE, CONSERVATION ACTIONS. THIS WILL WORK BEST IF ALL THE STAKEHOLDERS COLLABORATE TOGETHER TO ENSURE THAT THEY MAXIMISE OPPORTUNITIES FOR SYNERGY AND LEARNING ACROSS COUNTRIES, STAGES IN THE SUPPLY CHAIN, AND STAKEHOLDER TYPES. FUNDING FOR SPECIES CONSERVATION IS OFTEN DISPERSED ON A PROJECT-BY-PROJECT BASIS, AND AWARDEES FOCUS ON FULFILLING THEIR OWN AIMS AND MEETING THEIR DELIVERABLES - THEREBY LOSING THE OPPORTUNITY TO ENGAGE ACROSS PROJECTS, AND TO LEARN FROM EACH OTHER. ADDITIONALLY, SHORT-TERM PROJECT FUNDING CAN LEAD TO EXCELLENT RESULTS BUT NEW EVIDENCE CAN BE KEPT WITHIN THE TEAM ITSELF, SO OPPORTUNITIES ARE LOST TO USE IT AS A FOUNDATION FOR ONGOING LEARNING AND EVIDENCE-GENERATION BY THE BROADER CONSERVATION COMMUNITY. FINALLY, INVESTMENT IN CAPACITY-BUILDING FOR TEAM MEMBERS IS VITAL. HOWEVER, OPPORTUNITIES TO EXTEND THIS INVESTMENT BEYOND THE PROJECT TEAM TO SUPPORT PEOPLE IN OTHER COUNTRIES, SECTORS, AND PARTS OF THE SUPPLY CHAIN, ARE NOT ALWAYS GRASPED - THEREBY LIMITING THE EXTENT OF ITS IMPACT. THERE S AN OPPORTUNITY TO DO THINGS DIFFER</narrative>
  </description>
